From e0cd688c40b9e8ce253792d264e509c03d9dd2bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:00:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): session-scoped RPCs route to the owning gateway
 and follow it on not-found [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With several registry gateways, a stale owner record (a `local` hint minted
while the selected gateway fabricated rows for foreign ids, or a tile route
saved before the owner was known) outranks the MacBook-tagged row in the
unified list. Every session-scoped RPC then went to the wrong backend:
the mini's gui.log shows slash.exec / session.activate / process.list /
session.control.read rejected "not in memory" (4001) every 5s.

The shared router (requestForSessionProfile — the window dispatcher, the
store pollers via requestForOwnedSession, tile actions) now takes a
follower registered by owner-follow:

- pre-dispatch: a connection-tagged unified-list row naming another
  registered gateway, or an owner already proven by a follow, overrides the
  stale route
- on 4007 (stored id unknown there) look the owner up (rows, hints, by-id
  probe); on 4001 only rows/hints (a reaped runtime on its real owner
  answers 4001 too). Retry ONCE there; on success pin the hint, repoint the
  tile and memo the correction so the wrong gateway is not polled again
- a miss or failed retry is negative-cached for 60s per session/gateway,
  lookups are deduped, so a gone session costs one request per tick
- session.resume is excluded (its callers rebind to the owner themselves);
  fewer than two registry connections makes the follower inert
